      "state": "closed",
      "title": "feat(web,server): add a project to another machine from Run on, .env files included",
      "body": "Getting a repo from one machine onto another meant a manual clone, then copying `.env` and other gitignored files by hand. The \"Run on\" menu only lists machines that already have the project, so there was no way to start that from the place you pick a machine.\n\nNow \"Run on\" has a faded \"Add to another machine ›\" item. Hover it and pick a connected machine. A dialog shows source → target, lets you pick SSH or HTTPS and the folder, and lists the source's gitignored files with `.env*` checked. It clones with the existing tracked clone (same progress, cancel and retry toasts). After the clone fini…",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/pull/22180",
      "user": {
        "login": "t3dotgg",
        "type": "User"
      },
      "created_at": "2026-10-20T07:05:30Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-20T07:33:16Z",
